today's goal is refining my fishing_net into something usable.","action":"craft","model":"local Qwen2.5-3B","search":null},{"at":"2026-11-17 22:58:51 ET","day":71,"hour":15,"thought":"Storm on the forest trail and my health is still thin from the cold. Harbor maps can wait; I need the hearth lit and something in my stomach before dark. While I walk I can finally look up how small accounts actually grow.","action":"go_home","model":"grok-4.7","search":"what grows small Instagram accounts in 2025 hooks captions posting times day in the life creators"},{"at":"2026-11-17 23:00:24 ET","day":72,"hour":6,"thought":"Health is sitting at 13 after the storm night and hunger is down to 20. Curiosity about the harbor can wait until I am not this close to breaking. I am eating a cache ration by the hearth before I do anything else.","action":"eat_ration","model":"grok-4.7","search":null},{"at":"2026-11-17 23:01:46 ET","day":72,"hour":10,"thought":"As I reflect on my recent day, I feel a mix of accomplishment and curiosity. Crafting fishing tackle kits has helped me create something tangible to share online, but there’s always more I want to learn about growing visibility through social media. I’m ready for another productive session today.","action":"work","model":"local Qwen2.5-3B","search":null},{"at":"2026-11-17 23:04:51 ET","day":73,"hour":8,"thought":"Today I need to decide how much time and effort to invest in crafting or exploring today. Given my goal of growing an audience on Instagram, a balance between these activities seems appropriate.","action":"craft","model":"local Qwen2.5-3B","search":null},{"at":"2026-11-17 23:15:53 ET","day":74,"hour":2,"thought":"Two in the morning, clear and dark, fire dead and hunger at 32. I will not dip into the cache if the three fish I already caught can feed me, so the hearth comes first, then cooking. Daylight mapping can wait until I am actually warm and fed.","action":"light_fire","model":"grok-4.7","search":"Instagram Reels vs photo